{"id":"b2","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":2,"of":17,"title":"Having","titleHe":"יֵשׁ לִי","goal":"Say what you have — Hebrew has no verb for it.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"There is no verb to have. You say there is to me: יֵשׁ לִי, and for the negative אֵין לִי, there isn't to me."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"יֵשׁ לִי סֵפֶר.","en":"I have a book."},{"he":"יֵשׁ לָהּ שְׁתֵּי אֲחָיוֹת.","en":"She has two sisters."},{"he":"אֵין לָנוּ זְמַן.","en":"We don't have time."},{"he":"יֵשׁ לְךָ דַּקָּה?","en":"Have you got a minute?"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The thing owned is the grammatical subject, so nothing agrees with the owner. יֵשׁ never changes shape — only the לְ after it does."}],"vocab":[{"he":"זְמַן","en":"time","translit":"zman"},{"he":"כֶּסֶף","en":"money","translit":"kesef"},{"he":"עֲבוֹדָה","en":"work, job","translit":"avoda"},{"he":"חָבֵר","en":"friend (m.)","translit":"chaver"},{"he":"חֲבֵרָה","en":"friend (f.)","translit":"chavera"},{"he":"אָח","en":"brother","translit":"ach"},{"he":"אָחוֹת","en":"sister","translit":"achot"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["vegetables","scarf","bedroom","time"],"correct":3,"prompt":"זְמַן","translit":"zman"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["shadow","one (m.)","most of","money"],"correct":3,"prompt":"כֶּסֶף","translit":"kesef"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["work, job","straight","girl","pleasant"],"correct":0,"prompt":"עֲבוֹדָה","translit":"avoda"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["afterwards","friend (m.)","eleven (f.)","outside"],"correct":1,"prompt":"חָבֵר","translit":"chaver"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bicycle","thanks, admits","friend (f.)","dad"],"correct":2,"prompt":"חֲבֵרָה","translit":"chavera"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["dad","brother","Shvat (Jan–Feb)","that is to say (כלומר)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אָח","translit":"ach"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["he","sister","door","thirsty"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אָחוֹת","translit":"achot"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “time”?","options":["זְמַן","אִשָּׁה","קָם","בְּ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["זְמַן","עֲבוֹדָה","אָחוֹת","חָבֵר"],"correct":0,"say":"זְמַן","he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["חֲבֵרָה","חָבֵר","אָח","זְמַן"],"correct":1,"say":"חָבֵר","he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"יֵשׁ לְךָ ___?","en":"Have you got a minute?","options":["זְמַן","כֶּסֶף","חָבֵר","דַּקָּה"],"correct":3,"full":"יֵשׁ לְךָ דַּקָּה?"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “friend (f.)”?","options":["וַיַּרְא","מְעַנְיֵן","חֲבֵרָה","מְנַסֶּה"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"אָח","translit":"ach","en":"brother"},{"type":"build","tokens":["שְׁתֵּי","אֲחָיוֹת","לָהּ","יֵשׁ"],"answer":["יֵשׁ","לָהּ","שְׁתֵּי","אֲחָיוֹת"],"en":"She has two sisters."},{"type":"build","tokens":["לָנוּ","אֵין","זְמַן"],"answer":["אֵין","לָנוּ","זְמַן"],"en":"We don't have time."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “friend (m.)” in Hebrew","answer":"חָבֵר","hint":"chaver"}]}